    "rationale": "A is a network meta-analysis finding that SBP reduction with once-weekly semaglutide 1.0 mg was not statistically differentiable from SGLT-2 inhibitors at 26 (±4) weeks. B is the oral-route subgroup of a pairwise meta-analysis (a secondary finding): WMD -2.50 mmHg (95% CI -3.48 to -1.53) versus placebo or other antihyperglycaemic agents. Extraction gaps do not change either finding: stated aims are missing on both sides, A lacks the 'Compared with' field, the baseline starting time and the trial duration (>=20 weeks), and B lacks the comparison group in the groups row. The reference groups differ (a specific active class versus pooled placebo/other agents), so the two findings answer different questions. Route also differs (once-weekly versus oral), and the two meta-analyses may share trials, which the abstracts do not let me establish."
